body:
Love is to look up at the sky,
which in two eyes has fit entire,
and to fill the void inside your soul,
as no one else will ever manage.

Love is a stroke through the hair,
teasing you while you keep on whining,
getting lost in every hug of yours,
and flying high, each time you look at me.

Grant me a dance tonight, my heart,
and hold me tight, with you alone.
"What is love," softly sing to me;
tonight I became the man of your life.

Love is a coffee and a kiss;
a goodnight whispered in the dark;
a sorry locked inside a cell;
a forgiveness for your every flaw.

Love is waking up every morning;
gazing at you sleeping every night;
having your cool breath revive me;
being lulled to sleep by your touch alone.

Grant me a dance tonight, my heart...

Love is, to be honest,
a verse written on a scribbled paper;
love songs, my dear, you'll find plenty,
but this one right here is dedicated to us.
